From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Myles Liu <lyx981mike@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 15:58:30 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] qualcommax: ipq50xx: redmi-ax3000: allow holding the boot
 confirmation

A boot that U-Boot is trying after an upgrade is confirmed at the end of
init. Skip that when /var/run/xiaomi-dualboot.hold exists, so that an
updater can keep the new firmware on trial until the user (or a health
check) accepts it. An unconfirmed trial rolls back on the next reset.
---
 .../qualcommax/ipq50xx/base-files/etc/init.d/xiaomi-dualboot   | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/target/linux/qualcommax/ipq50xx/base-files/etc/init.d/xiaomi-dualboot b/target/linux/qualcommax/ipq50xx/base-files/etc/init.d/xiaomi-dualboot
index 23432931..b9ef12dd 100755
--- a/target/linux/qualcommax/ipq50xx/base-files/etc/init.d/xiaomi-dualboot
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommax/ipq50xx/base-files/etc/init.d/xiaomi-dualboot
@@ -5,6 +5,9 @@ START=99
 boot() {
 	case $(board_name) in
 	xiaomi,redmi-ax3000)
+		# Something else (e.g. an OTA updater's trial) confirms this boot
+		[ -e /var/run/xiaomi-dualboot.hold ] && return 0
+
 		. /lib/functions/xiaomi-dualboot.sh
 		xiaomi_dualboot_confirm
 		;;
